Right now there's already a problem with "bad" items such as rings, 
scrolls, potions, and wands -- the price ID technique doesn't require 
you to spend any resources to identify them within a small range. 
Amulets are the exception, I believe.

[I think this is actually a design problem with vanilla Nethack; the 
fact that a properly, _carefully_ played character can almost always 
ascend, because it's too easy to avoid all the minor badnesses that can 
befall such a character -- and the endgame is easy with adequate 
preparation, and there's plenty (endless?) time to prepare.  But that's 
another thread.]

