Putrid.

> Just a thought anyway. Please feel free to flesh it out as you see fit.

I see fit to throw it out.

Honestly, Nethack is a game where every keystroke can matter.  Confusion 
and stunning can kill in many wrong situations; and you want to add an 
effect that causes you to remove armor and unwield weapons, possibly 
throw them at people, and make random attacks?  At least with confusion 
and stunning you can choose to hit "." or (a)pply your unihorn until the 
effect fades -- and it looks like you'd disallow "." to rest and avoid 
making wrong attacks/steps with this idea.  Making this not curable by 
unicorn horn simply means that strong characters would now have yet 
another way to get instakilled, and possibly one totally out of their 
control.

If you DO make this curable by unicorn horn, it becomes something (like 
sickness and food poisoning) that has almost no effect on the game -- as 
soon as you become enraged, you (a)pply the horn, because any turns 
taken mean you could die or something horrible could happen (you tear 
your cloak, etc).  So instead of a super-complex effect with levels of 
shading and intrigue, you get an effect that lasts for 2 turns, tops, OR 
is Yet Another Way for low-level characters (who don't have a unicorn 
horn) to die suddenly or lose valuable equipment.

